Original commit body from 7b81a70:

Allows sketch to use a pre-computed hypergumbo.results.json file
instead of re-running analysis. This significantly speeds up
iterating on different token budgets for large codebases.

Features:
- New --input argument for sketch command
- Uses cached profile from results file (no re-detection)
- Uses cached symbols/edges from results file
- Staleness warning when source files are newer than results
- -x flag filters test symbols/edges from cached results

Also adds from_dict methods to Edge, Span, Symbol, LanguageStats,
and RepoProfile for reconstructing objects from cached JSON.

Updated USE-CASES.md with documentation and command aliases.
